            "89ebb234-da99-4e5b-ae43-e2739b386925": {
                "id": "89ebb234-da99-4e5b-ae43-e2739b386925",
                "createdAt": "2025-10-22T18:46:38.233Z",
                "parent": "bf54bfca-3bd8-4b41-9e84-4dd0671bf986",
                "type": "principle",
                "scope": "enterprise",
                "status": "published",
                "authors": [
                    "Bo"
                ],
                "title": "EAP 1: Functional Boundaries and Organisational Flexibility",
                "principle": "### Statement\nTo achieve clear functional boundaries, **Draftsman products are designed as separate systems**.\n\n### Rationale\nThis separation provides **organisational flexibility**, allowing each product to evolve independently — both technically and legally.\nFor example, we can use separate legal entities (\"rechtsvormen\") for different products, enabling isolation where needed.\n\n### Implication / Acceptance\nWe accept that this design prevents us from **bundling our software** (e.g. *“pay once and access both Tracepaper and Workbench”*).\nEach product must therefore justify its own value proposition and pricing model.",
                "sections": [],
                "prio": 0,
                "updatedAt": "2025-10-22T18:47:28.356Z"
            },
            "a201f648-b359-4621-b45c-8ea40b4d76e3": {
                "id": "a201f648-b359-4621-b45c-8ea40b4d76e3",
                "createdAt": "2025-10-22T19:18:23.823Z",
                "parent": "bf54bfca-3bd8-4b41-9e84-4dd0671bf986",
                "type": "principle",
                "scope": "enterprise",
                "status": "published",
                "authors": [
                    "Bo"
                ],
                "title": "EAP 2: We prefere serverless technologies",
                "principle": "### Statement\nTo ensure scalability and reduce operational overhead, **we prefer serverless technologies** over self-managed infrastructure.  \nThis principle guides our architectural choices toward services that automatically scale and minimize maintenance effort.\n\n### Rationale\nServerless platforms allow teams to focus on business logic instead of infrastructure management.  \nThey support **cost efficiency**, **automatic scaling**, and **fine-grained billing**, aligning with our goal of lean, adaptive systems.  \nWhile serverless imposes vendor constraints, its benefits in speed and autonomy outweigh those trade-offs for most workloads.\n\n### Implication / Acceptance\nWe accept that this preference limits our ability to deploy in certain on-premise or multi-cloud environments.  \nTeams choosing non-serverless options must explicitly justify their decision and document how operational risks are mitigated.",
                "sections": [],
                "prio": 0,
                "updatedAt": "2025-10-22T19:21:10.023Z"
            },
